---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Ethan Fang, Tennis Coach" description="Ethan Fang's tennis history — competitive junior player, private coach, and CWRU Club Tennis.">
  <article class="post container">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back</a>

    <header class="post__header">
      <h1 class="post__title">Ethan Fang, Tennis Coach</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="post__body">
      <p>
        I started playing tennis at the age of 7, and fell in love with the game. I competed in junior tennis at the highest level: reaching top 20 ranking in Northern California,
        playing several of the super national L1s, representing Team NorCal at Zonals, and reaching a peak UTR of 10. Along the way, I picked up partial sponsorships from Babolat, Solinco, and Adidas.
        I also played high school tennis, only losing 3 matches across 4 years, and earned 2nd place at NCS individuals my senior year.
      </p>
      <p>
        As my junior career winded down, I began coaching privately. spent 2021 and 2022 coaching privately, working with students who ranged from complete beginners
        to college players. I served as both a hitting partner and a coach, depending on what the student needed.
      </p>
      <p>
        In college, I chose to focus on acadeics. I attended Case Western, and wanted to serve my tennis community. I helped grow club tennis from 20 members to 120 and 
        secured a team sponsorship with Solinco. We set record practice attendances, and sign-ups would fill up in under 9 seconds whenever they were released every week.
        I cofounded the Cleveland Classic Club Tennis tournament with Cleveland State University in 2023, which has run annually for 3 consecutive years and allowed hundreds
        of club players across the country to come out and compete in Cleveland. I played mostly recreationally in college, but still competed in club tournaments with friends.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nowadays, I like to help out in my community through coaching junior players in the East Bay. I do private lessons and hitting sessions, so please reach out if interested!
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .post {
    padding: 4rem 0 6rem;
    width: min(100% - 2.5rem, 720px);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    background-image: none;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    transition: color 180ms ease;
  }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--accent); }

  .post__header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .post__title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .post__body {
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .post__body p {
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin: 0 0 1.1em;
  }
  .post__body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

</style>
